From 6ac11b8221a23889711d9f74af8b9cb0aba3ad63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 17:18:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add customer login and a real owner dashboard (Phase 5)

Restaurant owners can create a dashboard account right after checkout
completes (from /order/success, pre-filled with their checkout email) and
sign back in at /login. There is no public sign-up page - every account
starts from a real, completed Stripe checkout, verified server-side before
the account is created.

/dashboard is now gated by middleware the same way /admin already was
(separate tn_customer_session cookie, same jose/bcryptjs pattern as
lib/auth.ts, mirrored in the new lib/customerAuth.ts) and shows real data
from the orders table: order status, cards ordered, the Google review link
on file, and a working replacement-cards request form. The monthly AI
report panel is an honest "coming soon" placeholder, since that generator
and the Google review pull that would feed it don't exist yet (build item
#4, currently on hold per Isiah's decision to build his own data pull).

Schema: a new customers table (same shape as admin_users, kept separate so
an owner account can never get admin access) and a nullable
orders.customer_id, set at signup and backfilled by matching contact_email
so a restaurant that ordered before creating an account still sees that
order. No new environment variables.

Moved components/admin/StatusBadge.tsx to components/ui/StatusBadge.tsx
since the dashboard now needs it too, and removed data/sampleDashboard.ts,
which nothing references anymore now that the dashboard reads real orders.

See docs/14-phase-5-customer-dashboard.md for the full writeup, including
what this doesn't do yet (no password reset).

